  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Restaurant franchisee James Cain Sr. watched his business shift from doughnuts and baked goods towards beverages. His family's store renovations put pastries in prominent glass displays and introduced taps for cold drinks. Touch-screen ordering kiosks gave customers another way to order, while regular refurbishment was required by franchise agreements.\n\nFellow franchisees elected him to Dunkin's Brand Advisory Council, representing the New York region. The council met regularly with senior management to discuss marketing, menu development, technology and staff training. His participation gave an independent store operator a channel into decisions affecting the wider franchise network.",
